    "type": "question",
    "label": "49",
    "prompt": "Simplify the following algebraic fractions.\n$$\\frac{\\dfrac1a+\\dfrac1b}{\\dfrac1{a^2}-\\dfrac1{b^2}}$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\dfrac{ab}{b-a}$, for real $a,b$ with $a\\ne0$, $b\\ne0$ and $b\\ne\\pm a$.",
      "worked": "Multiply top and bottom by $a^2b^2$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{\\frac1a+\\frac1b}{\\frac1{a^2}-\\frac1{b^2}}&=\\frac{ab^2+a^2b}{b^2-a^2}\\\\\\frac{\\frac1a+\\frac1b}{\\frac1{a^2}-\\frac1{b^2}}&=\\frac{ab(a+b)}{(b-a)(b+a)}\\\\\\frac{\\frac1a+\\frac1b}{\\frac1{a^2}-\\frac1{b^2}}&=\\frac{ab}{b-a}\\end{align*}$$\nOriginal domain: real $a,b$ with $a\\ne0$, $b\\ne0$ and $b\\ne\\pm a$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 32
  },
